            "statement": "For every m in Sym6, the selected source (F6^2/16)m has the exact Cayley lift y_m=C0(F6+w^2)m*t2^3*s^2/16 in the dPhi/du block. The identity K(F6+w^2)+F6^2=w^4 leaves only C0*w^4*m, whose rows are disjoint from the selected 24767-row core, while the correction has zero u derivative and hence W*y_m=0. The 28 independent vectors therefore lie in the Q(gamma) kernel. Good reduction gives the opposite rank bound, so component0 has exact rank162. Replacing its structural increment190 by162 tightens the global Q rank interval to4748..5195.",
        },
        "frontier_delta": {
            "before": "Component0 had a geometrically identified 28-dimensional finite kernel but no characteristic-zero bordered annihilation; the global Q rank interval was4748..5223.",
            "after": "The exact Cayley lift promotes all28 component0 relations over Q(gamma), proves component0 rank162 and reduces the global upper bound by28 to5195. The remaining gap447 belongs to later ordered components.",
        },
        "next_required_object": "Apply the same source-first analysis to component9, whose finite rank169 versus structural increment252 contributes the next83 positive gap units. Search its normalized kernel for a common q79 Cayley/Koszul factor before any further prime campaign.",
    }
    OUT.write_text(json.dumps(packet, indent=2, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n", encoding="ascii")
    print("UST.G3DZ H02 component0 Cayley lift: PASS")
    print("component0_rank_Qgamma=162 global_Q_interval=4748..5195 remaining_gap=447")
